  "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Transportation_Problem\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    sources = list(range(10))  # S0..S9\n    destinations = list(range(9))  # D0..D8\n\n    supplies = [85, 61, 62, 33, 93, 83, 40, 43, 29, 24]\n    demands = [12, 70, 27, 60, 66, 52, 12, 55, 37]\n\n    # Cost matrix: rows correspond to sources S0..S9, columns to destinations D0..D8\n    costs = [\n        [ 29.11,  29.40,  11.53,   5.35,  13.10,  27.83,  15.26,   9.04,  12.05],  # S0\n        [ 22.65,  13.71,  17.59,  18.51,  20.25,  23.09,  19.51,  11.20,  28.49],  # S1\n        [ 11.29,  21.52,  11.55,  13.94,  20.15,  27.69,  18.66,  13.54,   6.18],  # S2\n        [  8.66,  11.40,   5.02,  22.47,  21.06,   7.18,  10.10,  11.44,  28.57],  # S3\n        [  6.90,  23.84,  22.63,  25.43,  15.33,  13.86,  12.40,  11.89,  14.84],  # S4\n        [  9.52,   8.80,  22.71,  21.74,  16.82,  27.68,   8.12,  18.98,  13.53],  # S5\n        [  8.07,  28.92,  15.48,  14.52,  19.63,  19.10,  20.61,  12.26,   8.46],  # S6\n        [ 26.35,   8.03,  20.27,   7.85,   6.40,  17.12,  19.17,   9.36,  15.45],  # S7\n        [  8.12,   8.88,  14.05,   9.86,  19.24,  12.78,  16.61,  19.75,  13.13],  # S8\n        [ 15.71,  25.21,  27.32,  26.54,  17.38,   8.13,   8.90,  26.16,  14.14],  # S9\n    ]\n\n    # Decision variables:\n    # Flow_S{i}_D{j} >= 0 is the quantity shipped from source i to destination j\n    flows = {}\n    for i in sources:\n        for j in destinations:\n            flows[(i, j)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_S{i}_D{j}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total transportation cost\n    m.setObjective(\n        quicksum(costs[i][j] * flows[(i, j)] for i in sources for j in destinations),\n        GRB.MINIMIZE\n    )\n\n    # Supply constraints: Shipments from each source <= its supply\n    for i in sources:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for j in destinations) <= supplies[i],\n            name=f\"Supply_S{i}\"\n        )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Shipments to each destination >= its demand\n    for j in destinations:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for i in sources) >= demands[j],\n            name=f\"Demand_D{j}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
  "LLM_description": "To: Operations, Finance, and Sales Leadership\nFrom: Supply Chain Director\nDate: [Date]\nSubject: Shipping plan to meet all destination needs at the lowest total cost\n\nSituation\nLogistics spend is a major driver of overall margin and a key contributor to on-time, in-full performance. We serve a network of destination locations from multiple source facilities, and shipping costs differ by route. Aligning the right flows across the network will reduce transportation spend, preserve service levels, and improve inventory utilization. Partial shipments are allowed, so we can split deliveries across routes when it makes sense.\n\nProblem\nWe need to determine how much product to ship from each source to each destination so that:\n- No source is allocated more than its available inventory or capacity.\n- Every destination\u2019s required quantity is met in full.\n- The overall transportation spend is as low as possible, given that costs vary by route.\n\nIn practical terms, the outcome should be a clear, lane-by-lane shipment plan that meets all requirements, leverages the cost differences across routes, and uses partial shipments where beneficial. This plan will serve as the basis for weekly execution and ongoing refresh as costs or availability shift.\n\nApproach\nUsing the data in the Annex, we will:\n- Confirm available supply by source, required demand by destination, and the per-route shipping costs.\n- Identify the lowest-cost combination of shipments that fulfills all destinations without exceeding any source\u2019s availability.\n- Validate the recommended plan with transportation scheduling and inventory teams, and prepare a routing guide and implementation cadence.\n\nAnnex \u2013 Shipping Data:\nDestination requirements: Store D1 needs 70 units; Store D2 needs 27 units; Store D0 needs 12 units; Store D4 needs 66 units; Store D6 needs 12 units; Store D8 needs 37 units; Store D3 needs 60 units; Store D5 needs 52 units; Store D7 needs 55 